shape theory.contact.self : theory.contact, theory.self-reference {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definition 5.2 (Self-Contact).
// By Theorem 3.7, every shape's transformation depends on its own
// prior character. This mandatory self-reference is self-contact:
// the shape in structural relationship with itself across moments.
// Self-contact is persistence itself: it is the contact between M
// and M' through which the shape endures.
//
// Self-contact is the minimal contact. It exists for every shape.
// A shape's internal structure is the geometry of its self-contact.
// Every shape must have internal structure because every shape must
// have self-contact. This is why persistence requires structure: not
// by additional axiom, but because persistence IS self-contact, and
// contact is a structural relationship.
//
// Derives from: theory.contact, theory.self-reference
  """
}
